---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '@/components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-09-15';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy: TTP">
  <Navbar />
  <main class="wrap-narrow pb-20 pt-16 text-muted">
    <h1 class="display mb-2 text-[clamp(2rem,1.4rem+1.8vw,2.75rem)] text-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mono mb-10 text-xs text-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="mb-6">
      TTP (Talk To Paste) is a desktop voice-to-text app. Transcription is not local: each
      recording is sent to Groq using an API key that belongs to you. This page describes
      exactly what stays on your computer and what leaves it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">What stays on your computer</h2>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-faint">
      <li><strong>Audio recordings</strong>: kept on disk only as a temporary backup while a transcription is in flight, then deleted automatically.</li>
      <li><strong>Transcription history</strong>: stored locally so you can copy past results. You can disable history or clear it from Settings at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Dictionary entries</strong>: corrections you've taught TTP. Local only.</li>
      <li><strong>Settings</strong>: your preferences (shortcut, hands-free mode, history toggle, etc.).</li>
      <li><strong>Licence state</strong>: if you bought the optional €17 licence (sound packs), a signed copy of it so the packs stay unlocked offline.</li>
      <li><strong>Groq API key</strong>: stored in the macOS Keychain. Never written to disk in plain text.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">What gets sent to third parties</h2>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-faint">
      <li>
        <strong>Groq</strong> (<a class="link" href="https://groq.com/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>):
        every audio recording is sent to Groq's Whisper endpoint to be transcribed.
        If AI correction is enabled (the default), the raw text is also sent to a Groq model to be cleaned up. If you turned on <em>screen context</em> (off by default), the names shown on screen that sound like what you said, and the sentence you are continuing, are sent with it. Password fields and password managers are never read, and nothing from the screen is kept.
        TTP does not store or access your Groq API key beyond the call itself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong> (<a class="link" href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>):
        handles payment if you buy the optional licence and validates your license key.
        Your billing information is processed by Lemon Squeezy, not TTP.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sentry</strong>: error reporting. <strong>Off by default.</strong> When you opt in (at the end of setup, or in Settings → Advanced), crash reports are sent to help fix bugs.
        API keys, file paths, email addresses, and the contents of your transcriptions are scrubbed before sending.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub</strong>: used as the auto-update channel. The app checks GitHub Releases for new versions and downloads them. No identifying information is sent.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">What we do not do</h2>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-faint">
      <li>We do not sell or share your data with anyone.</li>
      <li>We do not train models on your transcriptions. (Groq's policy on training applies independently: see their link above.)</li>
      <li>We do not run any analytics or telemetry by default. Both must be explicitly enabled.</li>
      <li>There is no tracking pixel, no advertising network, no third-party fingerprinting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">Your data, your control</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">All TTP data on your computer lives in:</p>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-faint">
      <li><code class="mono rounded border border-line bg-raised px-1.5 py-0.5">~/Library/Application Support/com.ttp.desktop/</code></li>
      <li><code class="mono rounded border border-line bg-raised px-1.5 py-0.5">~/Library/Application Support/ttp/</code></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-6">
      Settings → Advanced → Uninstall removes the app and all of this. Deleting these folders does the same by hand. No server-side state is held about you outside of the third parties listed above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      Questions, deletion requests, or issues:
      <a class="link" href="mailto:amirksmain@gmail.com">amirksmain@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="display mb-3 mt-12 text-xl text-text">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      Material changes will be announced in the changelog and a fresh "Last updated" date will appear at the top of this page.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
